ENTRY            D6419   20260916   20261124   20261124       D153
SUBENT        D6419001   20260916   20261124   20261124       D153
BIB                 11         28
TITLE      Systematic study of fusion suppression for tightly
            bound projectiles at above-barrier energies
AUTHOR     (M.S.Asnain, M.Shuaib, I.Majeed, M.K.Sharma,
            V.R.Sharma, A.Yadav, D.P.Singh, P.P.Singh, S.Kumar,
            R.Kumar, B.P.Singh, R.Prasad)
INSTITUTE  (3INDMUA,3MEXUMX,3INDIIR,3INDNSD)
           (3INDIND) Shri Varsheny College, Aligarh
           (3INDIND) Jamia Millia Islamia, New Delhi
           (3INDIND) University of Petroleum and Energy Studies,
            Dehradun Uttarakhand
REFERENCE  (J,PR/C,105,014609,2022)
           #doi:10.1103/PhysRevC.105.014609
FACILITY   (VDGT,3INDNSD) Pelletron ion-beam facility
SAMPLE     Spectroscopically pure thin 181Ta targets and
            aluminum catcher/energy-degrader foils were prepared
            by using the rolling technique.
DETECTOR   (HPGE) Detector with a 100 cm3 active volume and
            1.2 keV resolution at 1.33 MeV (60Co), calibrated
            using 22Na, 60Co, 133Ba, and 152Eu sources.
METHOD     (ACTIV,STTA)  Irradiation was carried out at 65-88 MeV
            with a 4-5 pnA beam current using 3 stacks each
            consisting of four target-catcher foil assemblies.
ANALYSIS   Summation of the production cross sections of
            192Hg(3n), 191Hg(4n), 190Hg(5n), 189Hg(6n),
            191Au(p3n), 190Au(p4n) and 189Au(p5n).
ERR-ANALYS (DATA-ERR) No information on sources of uncertainties
HISTORY    (20260913R) Data received from A. Yadav
           (20260916C) Paresh Prajapati - AASPP Workshop,2026
ENDBIB              28
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT           31
